</Field Guns Equipment>

<overview>
<p>Infantry equipped with microlite aircraft that are little more than a hang glider with a pusher prop engine can roam even the most restrictive terrain at will - providing the weather cooperates. The ultra-short take off and landing capability allows them to stage from areas that prohibit conventional aircraft, and their slower, highly maneuverable nature mean they can safely operate much closer to the ground, slipping around hills and through valleys unobserved. Weight limits restrict the use of heavy support weapons making them suited to observation and similar roles rather than direct combat.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date selected as generic early date, prior to most advanced infantry equipment
</notes>

